        "calls": 2,
        "title": "Cloud project types gain scratch origin and capability flag",
        "summary": "The shared desktop-cloud contract in `common` adds a `startedFromScratch` field to `CloudHistoryProject`, which is true when a user created the project empty in Freebuff, the only kind of project whose new chat offers templates. The same commit adds an optional `projectOrigin` capability to `deviceCapabilities` in `device-execution.ts`, allowing Desktop clients to signal support for accepting the scratch origin. These fields are optional and absent from older servers; `startedFromScratch` is false for chosen folders, GitHub repositories, templates, copies, and projects created before this tracking was added.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "The diff adds an optional `projectOrigin` boolean flag to the `deviceCapabilities` Zod schema in `common/src/desktop-cloud/device-execution.ts` and an optional `startedFromScratch` boolean field to the `CloudHistoryProject` type in `common/src/desktop-cloud/history.ts`.",
